eMatch 🛠️ Reuse the Jira Integration in a New Katalon Project

Created by CAVALHER Erica (EXT) on Mar 26, 2026

This page explains how to copy and configure the current Jira integration into a new Katalon project.

The objective is to allow another project to reuse the same publishing flow, including:
	•	Test Plan resolution
	•	Test Execution import
	•	execution update
	•	attachment upload
	•	custom HTML report generation
	•	controlled report steps
	•	controlled screenshot evidence

⚠️ Important context before reusing

This integration is designed for step by step Katalon test cases.

It is not a Gherkin / BDD flow.

To make the custom HTML report look correct and useful, the test cases must explicitly write the report steps using the dedicated keyword:
	•	CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Step text here')

If you want the report to show clean visual steps, you must use this controlled step call inside the test flow.

Automatic failure screenshots are handled by the integration, and additional manual evidence can also be captured when needed through the image keyword logic already included in the project.

To make the integration work in a different project, it is necessary to copy the integration classes and request objects, keep the expected structure, and update all project-specific values such as Jira base URL, project key, Epic key, labels, environment, report file names, logo, and naming rules used by the new automation suite.

⸻

📂 Files that must be copied to the new project

Copy the following Groovy classes into the new Katalon project under the same package structure, keeping the package name jiraIntegration unless you intentionally want to rename it and update imports accordingly.

Download folder OR copy manually
	•	JiraFlowCoordinator
	•	JiraGateway
	•	JiraTestPlanManager
	•	JiraExecutionPublisher
	•	JiraReportBuilder
	•	JiraHtmlTemplateBuilder
	•	JiraIntegration
	•	JiraImagesEvidence
	•	JiraReportSteps

Also keep only this active test listener:
	•	ematchReport

Do not use the old extra listener in the new reusable flow.

⸻

📂 Jira request objects that must be copied

Also copy the Jira request objects into the new project under the same Object Repository folder, or recreate them manually with the same names and payload structure.

Download folder OR recreate manually
	•	Jira Integration/Import Results
	•	Jira Integration/Create Test Plan
	•	Jira Integration/Update Test Plan
	•	Jira Integration/Update Test Execution Name
	•	Jira Integration/Evidence attachment

