🗂️ Recommended folder structure in the new project

To avoid changing more code than necessary, the easiest approach is to keep the same expected structure inside the new Katalon project.
	•	Groovy classes under package jiraIntegration
	•	Jira request objects under Object Repository/Jira Integration/
	•	report output under the project Reports folder
	•	logo asset under Image/logo.png
	•	local Test Plan key cache under TestPlanKeys/

Keeping this structure reduces the number of code changes required and makes migration faster and safer.

⸻

🚀 Minimum setup steps in the new project

To make the integration work in another project, the recommended setup order is:
	1.	Copy the integration classes
	2.	Copy or recreate the Jira request objects
	3.	Copy the report logo if the HTML report will still use it
	4.	Keep only the ematchReport listener active
	5.	Confirm the new project generates a supported XML result file
	6.	Update the configuration values inside JiraFlowCoordinator
	7.	Review Jira request object URLs and payloads
	8.	Test the flow with one suite only
	9.	Confirm that the Test Plan is created or reused correctly
	10.	Confirm that the Test Execution is created and updated
	11.	Confirm that the custom HTML report, Results.zip, and Evidences.zip are uploaded correctly
	12.	Confirm that the step list appears correctly using JiraReportSteps.note() inside the test case

