⚙️ Main file to configure first

The first file that must be updated in the new project is:
	•	JiraFlowCoordinator

This class contains the main integration configuration and controls the overall publishing flow. It is the central place where the new project identity, Jira mapping, naming, and file conventions should be adjusted first.

⸻

🔑 Variables that must be updated for the new project

Inside JiraFlowCoordinator, review and update at least the following values.

Jira connection and issue mapping
	•	JIRA_TOKEN
	•	PROJECT_KEY
	•	DEFAULT_EPIC_KEY
	•	JIRA_BASE_URL

These values are project-specific and must match the Jira instance and Jira project used by the new automation repository.

Execution metadata

Review in publisher / flow if applicable:
	•	environment
	•	labels
	•	execution naming rules

Optional behavior flags
	•	FORCE_CREATE_NEW_TEST_PLAN
	•	any local saved key reset strategy if introduced

Naming and file conventions

Review these concepts in the report and publisher flow:
	•	Test Plan suffix
	•	XML file names
	•	custom HTML report file name
	•	Results.zip name
	•	evidence folder naming
	•	Evidences.zip name

These must match the file outputs generated by the new project.

⸻

🧪 What the new project must generate for this integration to work

The integration expects that the project execution produces at least one valid XML result file.

By default, the current code looks for:
	•	JUnit_Report.xml

If the new project generates a different XML file name, update the logic in:
	•	JiraFlowCoordinator
	•	JiraReportBuilder

The integration also expects the report folder to contain execution artifacts and optionally evidence images saved in the expected structure.

