🧪 How to use in a non-BDD step by step project

This integration is meant for standard step by step Katalon test cases.

To make the report visually useful, you must explicitly log the steps you want to display.

Step keyword to use inside test cases

Use:
	•	CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Your step text')

Example:
	•	CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Open login page')
	•	CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Select environment')
	•	CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Validate current date')

Only these controlled notes are expected to become the clean visible steps in the report.

⸻

🖼️ How to use image evidence in test cases

Failure screenshots are automatically handled by the integration.

If the test also needs controlled evidence capture, review and use the image helper methods inside:
	•	JiraImagesEvidence

Typical usage should stay aligned with the controlled report structure so screenshots are linked to the correct scenario.

⸻

🧩 How to structure execution so Jira import works

To make the report generation and Jira publishing work correctly, the recommended structure is:

1. Create the real functional test suite

Example:
	•	Test Suites/PasserelleBilan/Passerelle Bilan H Bilan French IFRS

2. Create one dedicated Jira import test case

Example:
	•	Test Cases/Passerelle Bilan H Bilan French IFRS/Jira_Import_Passerelle Bilan

This test case should call:
	•	CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraIntegration.jiraImport'('EPIC-KEY')

3. Create one collection that runs both in order

Inside the Test Suite Collection, include:
	•	the real execution suite first
	•	the Jira import suite second

This is important because the Jira import flow needs the report artifacts already generated by the real suite execution.

Recommended collection order
	1.	Functional test suite
	2.	Jira import suite

That way, the second suite publishes the results of the first one.

⸻

🚨 Common reasons why the migration fails

The most common causes of failure when reusing this integration in another project are:
	•	wrong Jira token
	•	wrong Jira base URL
	•	wrong project key
	•	wrong Epic field mapping
	•	XML file not found because the new project uses another name
	•	evidence folder not matching the configured folder name
	•	request object URL still pointing to old Jira environment
	•	execution created but not linked to Test Plan due to Xray endpoint mismatch
	•	execution metadata update failing because the Jira field does not exist in the new project
	•	attachment upload failing because the file path is wrong or the file is empty
	•	report branding still pointing to old logo or old application name
	•	controlled report steps not appearing because JiraReportSteps.note() is not used in the test case
	•	wrong listener active instead of using only ematchReport

⸻

✅ Final recommendation

For the first migration, keep it simple:
	•	keep package name jiraIntegration
	•	keep only listener ematchReport
	•	reuse the same folder structure
	•	run one suite only first
	•	use JiraReportSteps.note() in the test case
	•	validate report generation before validating Jira publication
